@* The window's General holds Start-up and the main window's close button, and neither is the service's: Windows starts
   it as a service, and it has no window to close. Said, rather than an empty pane that looks like one failing to load. *@

<h2 class="label">General</h2>
<p class="hint">The service's own settings.json, under the Windows account it runs as. Saved, they apply to the next run; a run already going finishes on what it started with.</p>
<p class="hint">Start-up and the close button's action belong to the desktop app: Windows starts the service, and it has no window to close.</p>
